1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,000
Spain Stuns Argentina to Claim 2026 World Cup Crown.

2
00:00:04,950 --> 00:00:16,000
Spain etched its name into football history with a tense 1-0 victory over Argentina in the 2026 FIFA World Cup final at MetLife Stadium in East Rutherford, New Jersey.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:26,450
A second-half strike from Pedri was enough to separate the two sides in front of a packed crowd, many of whom had paid approximately $7,000 per ticket on the secondary market.

4
00:00:26,450 --> 00:00:36,075
The tournament marked the first edition of an expanded 48-team, 104-match format co-hosted by the United States, Mexico, and Canada.

5
00:00:36,075 --> 00:00:48,962
A record 3,605,357 spectators attended across the three host nations, with the United States staging 78 matches while Mexico and Canada each hosted 13.

6
00:00:48,962 --> 00:00:56,700
All three host nations advanced to the Round of 16, a remarkable achievement that underscored the growth of soccer across North America.

7
00:00:56,700 --> 00:01:05,400
The final itself was a tense, tactical affair, with Argentina's Lionel Messi unable to find a farewell goal in his last World Cup appearance.

8
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:12,412
Spain's victory capped a dominant campaign and signaled the emergence of a new European powerhouse on the global stage.

